"""Preparation-stage reference oracle for the FlagGems ``slogdet`` operator.

This file is the ``reference-as-solution`` candidate: it is injected through the
existing official override path (``--override slogdet:<this file>:run``) and is
therefore called with exactly the ABI the frozen accuracy test uses, i.e.
``flag_gems.slogdet(A) -> (sign, logabsdet)`` for ``A`` of shape ``(*, n, n)``.

Semantics preserved from the frozen Definition
(``definitions/slogdet.json``) and from the master test's own reference:

* ``sign`` keeps the input dtype (a unit-modulus complex number for complex
  input), ``logabsdet`` is the corresponding real dtype, both on the input's
  device and with shape ``A.shape[:-2]``.
* the input is never mutated and the outputs are freshly allocated
  (``effects.mutates == []``, ``effects.returns_alias_of == {}``).
* ATen's own rejection and autograd behaviour is kept: ``RuntimeError`` for
  fewer than 2 dimensions / non-square batches / low-precision dtypes /
  non floating-point-or-complex dtypes, and a differentiable ``logabsdet``.

It deliberately does not import ``flag_gems`` (and never names
``flag_gems.slogdet``), so this oracle cannot re-enter the overridden public
export and cannot act as its own candidate. ``torch.linalg.slogdet`` is used
unpatched: the pytest suites here never call ``flag_gems.enable()`` /
``use_gems()``, so no ``aten::slogdet`` kernel is replaced when this runs.
"""

import torch


def run(A):
    """Return ``(sign, logabsdet)`` with ``torch.linalg.slogdet`` semantics."""
    return torch.linalg.slogdet(A)
